{"title":"Operations Executive Roadmap","role":"Operations Executive","summary":"An Operations Executive is responsible for coordinating and improving day-to-day business or manufacturing operations. In an Industrial & Production Engineering context, the role focuses strongly on production planning, process coordination, inventory, quality, productivity, supply chain, and operational reporting.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Industrial & Production Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Operations Executive is responsible for coordinating and improving day-to-day business or manufacturing operations. In an Industrial & Production Engineering context, the role focuses strongly on production planning, process coordination, inventory, quality, productivity, supply chain, and operational reporting."},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate can enter operations in manufacturing, logistics, supply chain, e-commerce, automotive, FMCG, pharmaceuticals, electronics, or industrial services."},{"type":"h","text":"Core objective:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ensure that people, materials, machines, information, and processes work together efficiently, safely, and economically."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Operations Executive can develop toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Production Operations"},{"text":"Manufacturing Operations"},{"text":"Supply Chain Operations"},{"text":"Warehouse Operations"},{"text":"Logistics Operations"},{"text":"Procurement Operations"},{"text":"Quality Operations"},{"text":"Process Improvement"},{"text":"Lean Manufacturing"},{"text":"Business Operations"},{"text":"Operations Analytics"},{"text":"Project Operations"},{"text":"Plant Management"},{"text":"Operations Management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience, the career can progress toward Operations Manager, Plant Manager, Supply 