ational dashboards"},{"text":"Calculate operational KPIs"},{"text":"Identify process bottlenecks"},{"text":"Perform inventory analysis"},{"text":"Understand production planning"},{"text":"Apply Lean principles"},{"text":"Perform basic root-cause analysis"},{"text":"Work with ERP concepts"},{"text":"Use Excel at an advanced level"},{"text":"Write intermediate SQL queries"},{"text":"Build Power BI dashboards"},{"text":"Understand supply-chain processes"},{"text":"Communicate operational problems clearly"},{"text":"Present data-backed improvement recommendations"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an Industrial & Production Engineering student targeting Operations Executive, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Industrial Engineering","Operations Management","Lean","Supply Chain","Data Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Rather than becoming only a general operations graduate, the student should become an operations professional who can analyze data and improve processes."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended priority"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Production & Operations Management\n2. Advanced Excel\n3. Lean Six Sigma\n4. Supply Chain & Inventory\n5. Power BI\n6. Operations Research\n7. SQL\n8. ERP/SAP\n9. Python for analytics\n10. Internship + measurable operations project"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination provides multiple entry points into manufacturing, supply chain, logistics, business operations, process improvement, and operations analytics."}]}]}